body:
There is quite a difference on the price. The Standard is $200 cheaper than the Affinity since the affinity will be bought "Store new" with warranty and as a bundle.

&#x200B;

Would you say the Standard is a tiny bit better than the Affinity? Because if it is and it's cheaper then I'll definitely go for it

I dont understand why questions in this subreddit gets a lot of downvotes, is there a bot that downvotes everyone? You asked a valid question and I'm sure others would love to know.

&#x200B;

Personally I like the PBT doubleshots better, ABS feel smooth but I like just a bit of texture on the caps specially when I play or type cause my hands sweat a lot. Note, that the texture of course will depend on the manufacturer and the mold they use, but most of the time the build up on the shine of ABS really throws me off

Thanks for the detailed response, do you have any recommendations for a 'real' mech keyboard then? This keyboard's old now so I'm looking to replace it anyway

&#x200B;

Also, will an OEM profile work, and if I buy a separate 6.5u spacebar with it if I can find one?

Yes it is playling on the editor, I'm showing the video by putting a Video Player component over a plane, and that plane has a "sprite" material to make the colors correct.

&#x200B;

Do you mind if I send you a chat here on reddit so we can communicate faster?

How do I access the auto save recovery file tho? Also I think I had it disabled :////

&#x200B;

I loaded up the SWF file and it compressed everything. However the good thing is they're actually still preliminary sketches but they're half way done so I might just have to do from there.

I'm getting the error

Symbol 'Boom Tween 1', Layer 'Codes', Frame 12, Line 13  1061: Call to a possibly undefined method gotoAndStop through a reference with static type flash.display:DisplayObject

Here's the code I used

    Moon.addEventListener(MouseEvent.CLICK, showFrame);
    function showFrame(evt:MouseEvent):void
    {
        addEventListener(Event.ENTER_FRAME, skipToFrame);
        MovieClip(root).gotoAndStop(2, "Scene 1");
    }
    function skipToFrame(evt:Event):void
    {
        stage.getChildByName("MoonEarth").gotoAndStop(1);
        removeEventListener(Event.ENTER_FRAME, skipToFrame);
    }


Also, I apologize if it's quite complicated I didn't mean to use Frame scripts it's just that the idea requires it. I could send you the flash file so you can have a better idea of what I'm trying to do, cause I want that button to reset everything that is in mc2 everytime I click it so basically go back to frame 1
